# Resonantia C++ Style Guide (Google C++ Style + Project Extensions)

## Language
- **C++20** standard
- **CUDA 20** standard for `.cu` files

## Naming Conventions

| Element | Convention | Example |
|---------|-----------|---------|
| Files | `snake_case` | `hubert_encoder.h`, `cuda_flat_index.cu` |
| Namespaces | `snake_case` | `voxmutatio::content` |
| Types/Classes | `PascalCase` | `HubertEncoder`, `AudioBuffer` |
| Functions | `snake_case` | `extract_features()`, `init()` |
| Variables | `snake_case` | `num_samples`, `sample_rate` |
| Members | `snake_case_` (trailing underscore) | `output_dim_`, `half_precision_` |
| Constants | `kPascalCase` | `kHubertHiddenDim`, `kVitsSegmentSize` |
| Enums | `enum class` with `kPascalCase` values | `ModelVersion::kV1` |
| Macros | `K_SNAKE_CASE` (avoid when possible) | - |

## Header Guards
- Use `#pragma once` for all headers

## Namespace Style
- Use single-line nested syntax (C++17):
  ```cpp
  namespace voxmutatio::content {
  // ...
  }  // namespace voxmutatio::content
  ```

## Constexpr & Static Assert (宪法治理)
- Use `static_assert` for compile-time validation:
  ```cpp
  static_assert(kHubertHiddenDim == 768U);
  static_assert(sizeof(AudioBuffer) == expected_size);
  ```
- Use `constexpr` for compile-time computation
- Use `[[nodiscard]]` on all value-returning functions
- Use `noexcept` on non-throwing functions

## Number Literals
- Use C++14 digit separators: `16'000`, `40'000`, `3200U`
- Use `U` suffix for unsigned: `256U`, `768U`

## Includes
- Order: system headers → third-party → project headers
- Use quotes for project headers: `#include "voxmutatio/core/types.h"`

## Formatting
- See `.clang-format` for automatic formatting rules
- 4 spaces for indentation (no tabs)
- 100 character line limit

## CUDA Specific
- `.cu` files for device code
- `.cuh` files for device headers (internal use)
- Use `__device__`, `__host__ __device__` qualifiers appropriately
- Use `cudaMalloc`/`cudaFree` or custom allocator from `core/allocator.h`
